## 3. P1 — Structural and correctness risks

### P1-1　Non-monotonic section order ⇒ cross-reference drift in shared files

Companion order: `sec1, secsc, sec2, sec3, sec4, secgr, sec8, sec9, secscale, sec5, sec6, sec7`.

Assuming one `\section` per file (**verify**), the same shared file lands on different numbers in the two documents:

| Shared file | Section # in `main` | Section # in companion | Shift |
|---|---|---|---|
| `sec2` | 2 | 3 | +1 |
| `sec3` | 3 | 4 | +1 |
| `sec4` | 4 | 5 | +1 |
| `sec5` | 5 | 10 | **+5** |
| `sec6` | 6 | 11 | **+5** |

Because theorems are numbered `[section]`, **every hard-coded "Section 5" / "Theorem 6.2" inside the shared files is correct in at most one document.** Mandatory action: grep the subfiles for hard-coded numbers and convert to `\label`/`\ref` (or `cleveref`). Also note `sec8.tex` will render as Section 7 — filenames no longer encode order, a maintenance trap.

### P1-2　Remaining engineering issues (both masters)

| # | Issue | Action |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `\emergencystretch=3em` present in `main.tex`, **absent here** | Unjustified preamble drift; restore it (long math + `11pt` ⇒ overfull hboxes) |
| 2 | No `\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}` with `lmodern` | Add before `lmodern`; OT1 breaks hyphenation/PDF text extraction |
| 3 | `\newcommand{\T}` | May clash with `babel`/language packages (`already defined`); prefer `\TT` |
| 4 | `tabularx` + `longtable` | Cannot nest; use `xltabular` for breakable full-width tables |
| 5 | `placeins[section]` + `longtable` | Per-section `\FloatBarrier` can strand floats / create blank pages around long tables |
| 6 | `\input{bib}` type unknown | `thebibliography` ⇒ direct build; `\bibliography{…}` ⇒ BibTeX/Biber pass required |
| 7 | TOC + `hyperref` + section-numbered theorems | ≥2 passes; use `latexmk` |
| 8 | Duplicate `\label`s across 13 inputs | Merged/inserted sections (`secsc`, `secgr`, `secscale`) are prime suspects; check the log |
| 9 | `pdfauthor={Anonymous}` | Confirm no deanonymizing content in the shared `sec1` (acknowledgements, grants, self-citations) |

