## 6. Detection / repair / verification

The recursive scanner supplied in the previous audit applies **unchanged** to this file and to all 16 subfiles (it already covers `ewtheorem|ewcommand|ewpage|ewline|oindent|onumber|otag|abla|otin|…`, dry-run by default, `.tex.bak` backups on `--fix`).

Quick triage and build gate:

```bash
# 1. confirm the damage exists on disk (not just in transit)
grep -nE '^(ew|oindent|onumber|otag|abla|otin)' *.tex        # expect empty after repair

# 2. which macros do the shared sections actually need?
grep -ohE '\\(lrc|taust|Vol)\b' sec1.tex sec2.tex sec3.tex sec4.tex sec5.tex sec6.tex | sort | uniq -c

# 3. hard-coded cross-references that break under the +1/+5 section shift
grep -nE '(Section|Theorem|Lemma|Corollary|Proposition)~?[0-9]+\.[0-9]+' sec*.tex

# 4. duplicate labels across the 13 inputs
grep -ohE '\\label\{[^}]+\}' sec*.tex | sort | uniq -d

# 5. build both masters in isolated output dirs
latexmk -pdf -outdir=build_neg -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error main.tex
latexmk -pdf -outdir=build_psl -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error main_companion.tex
grep -nE "Undefined control sequence|not found|Missing .begin|already defined|multiply defined" build_*/*.log
```

**Prevention:** write TeX only via raw strings (`r"..."`), `Path.write_text()`, or template files — never let a string containing LaTeX pass through one round of `\n` escape interpretation.

